 "notes": [
  "Pig'Halle: not included - no own website found; OpenTable lists it at 38 South Street, the same address now used by Cardo, so it appears closed/replaced.",
  "The Sandeman (14-16 Kinnoull St, PH1 5EN): CAMRA lists it closed long-term since 25/06/2026 - excluded.",
  "Taythorpe is a guest house (no restaurant) - excluded. 'Fleming's' - no Perth venue found. Murrayshall skipped (outside city). Leonardo Boutique Huntingtower (Crieff Road, PH1) is a chain hotel on the outskirts - not researched.",
  "Cardo and Broth3rs sites have been fully relaunched since the last check (Cardo previously showed a 2021 COVID notice; Broth3rs previously returned no menu content) - both now confirmed trading with current 2026 menus.",
  "North Port and Kisa's sites previously timed out for WebFetch but loaded fine via TinyFish this round - both now confirmed trading with menu URLs opened directly.",
  "Breizh still links only a 2023 Christmas menu; no 2026 festive menu seen.",
  "Cridos Festive Menu 2026 only published as Facebook video.",
  "Parklands Christmas page (year not verified) still not fetchable, but a current September 2026 bistro menu PDF is now linked.",
  "Paco's: main menu PDF is dated May 2025 and its festive PDF is dated 2025 - no 2026 versions seen yet.",
  "No own website found for The Bothy, Mae Ping, The Venue. Blend site still shows no menu. Greyfriars (503 error on direct fetch, read via WebFetch) and Old Ship Inn: food service still unclear.",
  "Twa Tams site links the same PDF filenames as before; site redesigned (nav now just 'Student'/'Drinks Promos'/'Drinks') but underlying PDFs unchanged.",
  "Mae Ping exact street number not verified (postcode PH2 8NY from listings); no own website found.",
  "Jade Garden: old /menu path now redirects into /our-menus's JS menu switcher, so only the working /our-menus URL is kept.",
  "The BANK Bar menu page (thebankperth.com/menu) is a JS-rendered Wix page with no static text content - listed as html but could not confirm current dish content.",
  "Milas (new, added this refresh): Turkish/Mediterranean grill opened on Perth High Street 25 Sept 2026, sister to Milas Dundee; exact postcode not found (former Argos unit) and no Perth-specific menu page located yet.",
  "Coverage: 27 venues, short of the 30-45 target; further candidates: Slainte Bar, The Silvery Tay, Ormonds, King James, Royal George Hotel, Salutation Hotel.",
  "Second pass 2026-09-28 (late morning): added Jeet Christmas 2026, Camperdown Elm festive/Christmas Day/Boxing Day 2026, The Rule Christmas 2026 PDFs, Milas shared menu page (Perth), Bar 10 afternoon tea; Giddy Goose Christmas bookings notice.",
  "Refresh 2026-10-05: Cardo set menu replaced by new October 2026 set menu PDF (signal) and June 2026 drinks menu added; Breizh wine list PDF added (Christmas still only 2023 file); Cridos seafood menu (Facebook, July 2026) added; Jade Garden lunch menu added; 63 Tay Street next Sunday Lunch now 6 Dec; Paco's 'Paella Night coming soon' notice no longer on site (removed) and still no 2026 festive menu; Parklands still only September bistro PDF (signal cleared), Christmas page blank; Deans festive page says menu & pre-order sheet emailed in November; North Port festive menu confirmed (lunch 2c £40/3c £45, dinner £43/£48). Unchanged: Deans, Cafe Tabou, Broth3rs, Everest Inn, Tabla, Kisa's, Effies, Willows, Hinterland, Stone Cafe, Twa Tams, Milas. Old Ship Inn and Greyfriars sites still show no food. Greyfriars direct fetch 503 (read via WebFetch). No venues closed. New-opening check: only Lamesa (Filipino-Scottish, High Street, opened May 2025 per The Courier) found - not added (no own site/postcode, not new).",
  "Refresh 2026-10-12: Breizh now links a new Christmas 'Menu de Noël' PDF (year not stated; replaced the 2023 file); 63 Tay Street menus now point to dated sample PDFs (new 4-for-44 sample 16 Sep 2026); Cridos seafood and festive menus now hosted as images on own site (replacing Facebook links); Deans festive PDF now only linked from festive-meals page, Dec closure notice no longer shown (dropped); Milas menu URL narrowed to dinner-menu tab, Perth postcode still unknown (former Argos unit, High Street). Added The Postbox by Andrew Spence (80 George St, PH1 5LB, opened late Aug 2026). Signals cleared on Cardo May lunch/dinner; stale 'site relaunched/loads reliably' notices dropped. Unchanged: Cafe Tabou, Tabla, Everest Inn, North Port, Jade Garden, Paco's (still 2025 festive only), Kisa's, Parklands (Christmas page still blank), Effies, Willows, Hinterland, Stone Cafe, Twa Tams, BANK Bar. Blend, Old Ship Inn, Greyfriars still show no food menu. Broth3rs read via TinyFish (JS site). No closures found. Bulk HTTP link check unavailable (proxy blocks curl); links verified via page fetches.",
  "Second pass 2026-10-12 (late morning): Stone Cafe operator-procurement notice added; Milas Perth still has no FHIS record or Tripadvisor listing found."
